--
workspace:
== 1 ==
id = 1
name = ws_1
created_by : user10
==
--

--
workspace_members
== 1 ==
id = 100
ref: ws -> (id:1, name:ws_1)
ref user -> (10, user10)
role: admin
==
== 2 ==
id = 101
ref: ws -> (id:1, name:ws_1)
ref user -> (10, user10)
role: member
==
--

SELECT w.id AS workspace_id,
  w.name,
  wm.role,
  wm.joined_at
FROM workspace_members AS wm,
INNER JOIN workspaces AS w,
ON w.id = wm.workspace_id,
WHERE wm.user_id = $1,
ORDER BY wm.joined_at ASC;

- once the owner deletes his account 

- if an owner of a workspace deleted their account, Transfer ownership to the longest-standing member of the workspace, and set workspaces.created_by to that member as well (**note**: as the original owner is the longest standing member we should select the second longest standing member)
- if the workspace has only one member who is the owner, then it could be deleted simply.

- a workspace roles
  - if an owner makes another member owner he will lose his ownership and becomes a moderator.
  - a moderator can make upgrade another member to moderator.
  - a moderator cannot make demote another moderator to a member.
  - self demoting is not possible.
  - if a member leaves the workspace it should be removed from the workspace_members.
  - if an owner leaves a workspace, the ownership will be transferer.

